<title>SPAIN: Spain's CNMV restarts Hisalba share trade.</title>
<headline>Spain's CNMV restarts Hisalba share trade.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Share trading in Spanish cement group Hornos Ibericos Alba-Hisabla SA will restart on Tuesday, the stock market commission CNMV said on Monday.</p>
<p>Shares were suspended on December 4 pending further information on a bid by Holderbank Financiere Glaris Ltd, which owns more than 80 percent of Hisalba's capital, for the remaining shares.</p>
<p>Holderbank made bid of 1,600 pesetas per share to all minority shareholders.</p>
<p>The CNMV said Hisabla paid an interim dividend of 42 pesetas on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
